The attached image illustrates the transient inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 at the injection site. Panel A shows the time-course of various immune cell populations (neutrophils, macrophages, antigen-presenting cells, eosinophils, and monocytes) recruited to the injection site, highlighting a peak in neutrophils at 6 hours followed by a sustained increase in monocytes, macrophages, and APCs around day 2, which then resolves by day 21. Panel B, through confocal microscopy, visually demonstrates that AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) is internalized by MHCII-positive cells, Ly6C+ monocytes, and Mac-2+ macrophages, confirming cellular uptake by relevant immune cells.